      "side": 1,
      "message": "Given that you call the actual vendor hook below, there is not a lot of value in guarding all this with the _enabled() variant of the hook here anymore. `trace_android_rvh_try_fixup_sea()` itself will expand to a static key check + an indirect function call, so you should probably just call it here directly. And the user_mode() and is_el1_instruction_abort() logic can go in the vendor code.\n\nWdyt of something simple like below:\n\n```\nbool can_fixup \u003d false;\n...\ntrace_android_rvh_try_fixup_sea(far, esr, regs, \u0026can_fixup);\nif (can_fixup \u0026\u0026 fixup_exception(regs))\n        return 0;\n```\n\nThat means open-coding `is_el1_instruction_abort()` in your module, but it\u0027s simple enough for not being too much of a hassle.",
